1- Assign order to on duty courier (system) Jerome
ID:
UC-DLV-01
Title:
Assign order to on duty courier
Description:
When an order is marked as ready the system should offer the delivery to one idle on-duty courier based off the following rule:
shortest straight line distance from courier to restaurant, smallest courier id is the tie breaker.
Primary Actor:
System
Preconditions:
Order is marked as ready
One or more couriers are Idle (otherwise see UC-DLV-06)
Postconditions:
Delivery request is sent to the closest, in terms of straight line distance, courier, who can then accept or decline
The courier is Assigned and holds only this order
Inputs:
Restaurant location
All idle courier locations
Order information, including destination location
Outputs:
Delivery request sent to courier
Main Success Scenario:
An order is marked as ready
The system reads the stored location (longitude and latitude) of all idle couriers
The system calculates the straight line distance from each of those couriers to the restaurant
The system sends a delivery request to the closest courier, using the smallest courier id as a tie breaker.







