PRC UC
1- Compute order fare (Nadine)

ID:
UC-PRC-01
Title:
Compute order fare
Description:
The total fixed fare of each order is calculated and saved in its billing record. At checkout, as part of Place Order, PRC computes totalFare = SUM(unit price × quantity) + deliveryFee + serviceFee + smallOrderSurcharge, where the surcharge applies only when the subtotal is below the smallOrderThreshold. All values other than the order lines must come from the configuration file. PRC will record this amount as the order’s billing record when the order is placed (the total amount that the customer pays).


Primary Actor:
Customer
Preconditions:
A customer is logged in
The customer has selected items from an open restaurant
The configuration file contains : serviceFee, deliveryFee, smallOrderSurcharge, smallOrderThreshold
Postconditions:
The customer has seen the total fare
The placed order has a billing record holding its unit prices, subtotal, delivery fee, service fee, surcharge and total
No ledger entry exists yet
Inputs:
Order lines (menu item, unit price, quantity)
The pricing values (serviceFee, deliveryFee, smallOrderSurcharge, smallOrderThreshold)
Outputs:
Total itemized fare (subtotal, delivery fee, service fee, surcharge, total)
One billing record
One output console line (DASH)
Main Success Scenario:
The customer selects items and quantities from an open restaurant
The system reads the pricing values from the configuration file
The system computes the subtotal and applies the delivery fee, the service fee and, if the subtotal is below the threshold, the surcharge
The system displays the itemized fare
The customer places the order
The system saves the billing record with the order and logs the command










2- Record order charge (Nadine)

ID:
UC-PRC-02
Title:
Record Order Charge
Description:
When the order reaches a final state (Delivered | Rejected | Cancelled), PRC adds one ledger entry with that state, the order's timestamps and its total charge:
if delivered → total billing amount
if cancelled or rejected → 0$

Note that the total order fare is never recomputed, so an order's total cannot change.
Primary Actor:
ORD (Order & Restaurant Core)
Preconditions:
The order has a billing record
ORD has moved the order to delivered, cancelled or rejected and recorded the transition with an event id
The ledger has no entry for this order’s final state
Postconditions:
The ledger holds exactly one entry for this order's final state
The billing record is unchanged
Inputs:
Order id
Final state
Order timestamps
Billing record
Outputs:
One ledger entry
One output console line (DASH)
Main Success Scenario:
ORD moves the order to a final state
PRC checks that the ledger has no entry for that final state
PRC reads the total from the billing record, without recomputing it
PRC sets the charge to the total if the order was delivered, or to 0$ if it was cancelled or rejected
PRC saves the ledger entry with the final state, timestamps and charge
The system logs the entry to the output console
















